# Cuearr — Releases (mandatory for agents)

Releases do **not** happen on merge alone. Agents must create a release whenever shippable work lands on `main` and users would otherwise still see only an older tag.

## When to release (do it without waiting to be asked)

Cut a release after **any** of these is true on `main`:

1. A **roadmap batch** PR is merged (e.g. B1, B2, B3…).
2. User-visible behaviour ships: verify/split quality, packaging, Docker image behaviour, API/UI that operators rely on.
3. The session ends with `main` **ahead of the latest GitHub release tag** by shippable commits — and you merged or the user confirmed the work is done.

**Do not** skip the release because “docs only” if the batch also included code that operators run. Pure typo/doc PRs may stay unreleased.

**Do not** invent a release for WIP branches or unmerged PRs.

## Version bump (semver, `v*` tags)

| Bump | When |
|------|------|
| **MINOR** (`v0.1.0` → `v0.2.0`) | New batch / features (default after B1, B2, …) |
| **PATCH** (`v0.2.0` → `v0.2.1`) | Fixes only on top of the last release |
| **MAJOR** | Breaking CLI/API/config/data migrations that require operator action |

Always prefix tags with `v` (workflow trigger: `push` tags `v*`).

## How (account + commands)

1. `gh auth switch --user marcatos` and verify `gh api user --jq .login` → `marcatos`.
2. On up-to-date `main`: `git fetch --tags origin` and `gh release list`.
3. Choose next version; write notes (batches/issues closed, breaking changes, Docker tag).
4. Annotated tag on the merge commit and push:

```bash
git tag -a v0.X.Y -m "v0.X.Y — short summary"
git push origin v0.X.Y
```

5. Confirm workflow `release` succeeds (binaries + GHCR `ghcr.io/marcatos/cuearr:v0.X.Y` and `:latest`).
6. Update README **Status** line if it still cites the previous release.
7. Tell the user the release URL: `https://github.com/marcatos/cuearr/releases/tag/v0.X.Y`.

Do **not** use force-push on tags already published. Do **not** publish from the work account.

## Session checklist (end of shippable work)

- [ ] Latest release tag == intended ship commit (or newer release created)
- [ ] `gh release view` shows assets / notes
- [ ] README Status points at the new tag (if applicable)
